---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Why PHPRise exists, what it refuses to do, and how it is maintained."
  path="/about"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Small parts, held to a standard</h1>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
          PHPRise is an open source foundation for PHP. The name joins PHP with rise:
          the work of raising the floor of what a PHP codebase is allowed to look like.
        </p>

        <p>
          It started from a frustration that is common in the PHP ecosystem: frameworks
          that are excellent until you need to replace one piece, and then require you
          to replace all of them. The alternative we build here is the opposite —
          architecture made of parts small enough to be understood in one sitting and
          replaced without permission.
        </p>

        <h2>What we refuse</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Frameworks leaking into the domain layer.</li>
          <li>Repositories that cannot be classified as atom, assembly or application.</li>
          <li>Abstractions created before the second use case exists.</li>
          <li>Code that needs a comment to explain its indentation.</li>
          <li>Interfaces published without a contract.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How it is maintained</h2>
        <p>
          Everything lives in the
          <a href="https://github.com/phprise-foundation" rel="noopener">phprise-foundation</a>
          organization on GitHub, under the MIT license. Development happens in public:
          issues describe intent, pull requests describe the change, and the
          <a href="/manifesto">manifesto</a> settles disagreements.
        </p>

        <p>
          There is no company behind the code and no paid tier. The project is funded by
          the time of the people who use it.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          The fastest way to reach a maintainer is through an issue or discussion in the
          relevant repository. For anything that does not belong to a single repository,
          open one in the
          <a href="https://github.com/phprise-foundation/template/issues" rel="noopener">template</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
